{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0178XtwAuhcHexM4u3zg1m3B","type":"tool_result","content":"51f0996 run: role flags win over CLI flags, CLI fills in both roles\n1:# `redeye`\n51:- [`.redeye.json`](#redeyejson)\n70:## Install\n76:### Requirements\n84:### Install Dependency Skills\n110:command (the same role-string syntax as `.redeye.json`), validates each\n111:one, and writes the result to `.redeye.json`.\n137:## Example Workflow\n156:### Create Issues\n176:## Examples\n182:### Keep Your Machine Awake\n186:#### Mac OS\n191:### Claude Opus 4.6\n197:### Claude Opus 5.5\n203:### Claude Sonnet 5.5\n209:### Claude Haiku 5.5\n215:### Claude Fable 5.1\n221:### `pi` + OpenRouter model\n231:### `codex` + Luna\n237:### `codex` + Terra\n245:### Local Model With `pi`\n254:  \"providers\": {\n262:        \"supportsUsageInStreaming\": false,\n352:#### 1. Load the right model\n370:##### Qwen3 Coder Next -- 94% NPU\n380:##### Qwen3.6 35B A3B Turbo -- 45% NPU\n386:##### Qwen/Qwen3.6-27B\n395:##### GLM 4.7 flash -- 57% NPU\n405:#### 2. Run the Loop\n411:##### Qwen3.5-9B-Turbo\n424:##### Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-turbo\n432:##### Qwen3.6-27B-Turbo\n439:##### Huihui-Ornith-1.5-35B-A3B-abliterated-Turbo\n446:##### Qwen3.8-27B-heretic-ara-Turbo\n452:##### Ornith-1.5-35B-A3B-Turbo\n467:## `.redeye.json`\n486:| `implement` | yes | -- | Role string for the implementing agent. Same syntax as the CLI: `<provider> [-m model] [--effort level] [--max-turns n] [--prefer-subagent model]` |\n506:provider that does not support them is not an error -- redeye\n511:## Command Line Arguments\n517:| `[provider]` | no | -- | Agent harness to spawn (e.g. `claude`, `codex`, `pi`). Optional when `.redeye.json` sets `implement` -- the implement role's provider is used. A CLI provider overrides implement |\n528:| `--effort <level>` | no | -- | Starting effort/reasoning level. Each provider has its own ladder: `claude` supports `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, `max` (forwarded as `--effort`); `codex` supports `low`, `medium`, `high` (forwarded as `-c model_reasoning_effort=<level>`); `pi` supports `off`, `minimal`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, `max` (forwarded as `--thinking`). Omitted = provider default. Each retry steps up from here (see `--retries`) |\n529:| `--prefer-subagent <model>` | no | -- | `claude` only. Sets `CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL=<model>` for every claude agent redeye spawns (tickets, merge-conflict re-spawns, the reviewer and the fixer) and adds a prompt rule: hand read-only work (exploring the codebase, searching code, test runs with long output) to subagents, and make every edit and commit yourself. The reviewer gets the rule without the edit and commit line, since it never edits. `\"\"` is the same as omitting the flag. For `codex` and `pi` it is skipped with one warning at startup (`--prefer-subagent not supported by <provider>, skipping`). `--dry-run` prints `Prefer subagent: <model>`, or `(none)`. See [`--prefer-subagent` option](#--prefer-subagent-option) |\n535:### Notes\n571:  level one rung up the provider's ladder: without `--effort` the\n574:  provider's max (`max` for claude/pi, `high` for codex).\n577:  the second waits double that, and so on. This lets provider\n636:### `--spec <name>` option\n643:### `graph` command\n679:### `--prefer-subagent` option\n700:# Opus writes the code, Sonnet subagents explore and run tests\n703:# Cheaper subagents for searches and noisy test runs\n706:# A Sonnet main agent with Haiku subagents\n709:# Pin an exact model ID instead of an alias\n712:# dry run\n713:# Check the setting and the prompt rule without running anything\n717:Only the `claude` provider supports the `--prefer-subagent` flag.\n725:### Environment Settings\n733:## How It Works\n748:### Worktrees\n774:### Progress","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fe82aa-8f32-4a13-8174-61fa0bc9b8df","uuid":"264ad089-6b6c-4616-a081-50912e0186bb","timestamp":"2026-11-21T03:01:44.477Z","tool_use_resu