s `off`, `minimal`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, `max` (forwarded as `--thinking`). Omitted = provider default. Each retry steps up from here (see `--retries`) |\n529:| `--prefer-subagent <model>` | no | -- | `claude` only. Sets `CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL=<model>` for every claude agent redeye spawns (tickets, merge-conflict re-spawns, the reviewer and the fixer) and adds a prompt rule: hand read-only work (exploring the codebase, searching code, test runs with long output) to subagents, and make every edit and commit yourself. The reviewer gets the rule without the edit and commit line, since it never edits. `\"\"` is the same as omitting the flag. For `codex` and `pi` it is skipped with one warning at startup (`--prefer-subagent not supported by <provider>, skipping`). `--dry-run` prints `Prefer subagent: <model>`, or `(none)`. See [`--prefer-subagent` option](#--prefer-subagent-option) |\n535:### Notes\n571:  level one rung up the provider's ladder: without `--effort` the\n574:  provider's max (`max` for claude/pi, `high` for codex).\n577:  the second waits double that, and so on. This lets provider\n636:### `--spec <name>` option\n643:### `graph` command\n679:### `--prefer-subagent` option\n700:# Opus writes the code, Sonnet subagents explore and run tests\n703:# Cheaper subagents for searches and noisy test runs\n706:# A Sonnet main agent with Haiku subagents\n709:# Pin an exact model ID instead of an alias\n712:# dry run\n713:# Check the setting and the prompt rule without running anything\n717:Only the `claude` provider supports the `--prefer-subagent` flag.\n725:### Environment Settings\n733:## How It Works\n748:### Worktrees\n774:### Progress","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0178XtwAuhcHexM4u3zg1m3B","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFKzfusPoFNG1FNsWvf2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01V69rjtZRu1RtspVDNZce8Q","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 467,520p README.md; sed -n 1,50p README.md | grep -n \"redeye \" "},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1936,"cache_read_input_tokens":97938,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1936},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fe82aa-8f32-4a13-8174-61fa0bc9b8df","uuid":"1c8208b1-c242-4574-a21e-8ca84b0f3ce4","timestamp":"2026-11-21T03:01:46.251Z","request_id":"req_011ChFKzfkhdsYhszFsVJaPj","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01V69rjtZRu1RtspVDNZce8Q":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/redeye.adversarial-review-02-run-with-the-implement-role && sed -n 467,520p README.md; sed -n 1,50p README.md | grep -n \"redeye \" "}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01V69rjtZRu1RtspVDNZce8Q":{"cwd":"/Users/nick/code/redeye.adversarial-review-02-run-with-the-implement-role"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V69rjtZRu1RtspVDNZce8Q","type":"tool_result","content":"## `.redeye.json`\n\nAn optional config file at the repo root. When present with an\n`adversarial` key, each ticket goes through a cross-model review loop\nbefore it can merge.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"adversarial\": {\n    \"implement\": \"claude -m opus --effort high\",\n    \"review\": \"pi --effort medium\",\n    \"maxRounds\": 3,\n    \"minRounds\": 1\n  }\n}\n```\n\n| Field | Required | Default | Description |\n|-------|----------|---------|-------------|\n| `implement` | yes | -- | Role string for the implementing agent. Same syntax as the CLI: `<provider> [-m model] [--effort level] [--max-turns n] [--prefer-subagent model]` |\n| `review` | yes | -- | Role string for the reviewing agent |\n| `maxRounds` | no | `3` | Maximum review/fix rounds per ticket |\n| `minRounds` | no | `1` | Minimum rounds before a clean review can pass the ticket |\n\nA ticket passes when a round ends with no open findings and\nat least `minRounds` rounds have run. With `minRounds: 2`, a\nclean first round is followed by a second review before the\nticket merges. When the review in round `maxRounds` leaves\nfindings open, the ticket becomes `ready-for-human` (unresolved)\nwith its branch kept, and the fixer does not run after that\nfinal review.\n\nA missing file or a file with no `adversarial` key leaves\nbehavior unchanged. Invalid JSON, an `adversarial` value that\nis not an object, a missing role, or an invalid role string\nstops the run before any branch or worktree is created\n(exit 2).\n\nA role string with `--max-turns` or `--prefer-subagent` on a\nprovider that does not support them is not an error -- redeye\nwarns and drops the flag for that role, the same as the CLI\npath.\n\n\n## Command Line Arguments\n\nFlags:\n\n| Flag | Required | Default | Description |\n|------|----------|---------|-------------|\n| `[provider]` | no | -- | Agent harness to spawn (e.g. `claude`, `codex`, `pi`). Optional when `.redeye.json` sets `implement` -- the implement role's provider is used. A CLI provider overrides implement |\n| `[turns]` | no | -- | Max agentic turns per agent run (positional shorthand for `--max-turns`) |\n| `-m`, `--model` | no | -- | Model flag passed to the agent |\n| `--spec <name>` | no | auto | Feature name (resolves `.scratch/<name>/`) |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fe82aa-8f32-4a13-8174-61fa0bc9b8df","uuid":"177632a0-711e-4f7d-be64-e4d1a8e5c5f0","timestamp":"2026-11-21T03:01:46.331Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## `.redeye.json`\n\nAn optional config file at the repo root. When present with an\n`adversarial` key, each ticket goes through a cross-model review loop\nbefore it can merge.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"adversarial\": {\n    \"implement\": \"claude -m opus --effort high\",\n    \"review\": \"pi --effort medium\",\n    \"maxRounds\": 3,\n    \"minRounds\": 1\n  }\n}\n```\n\n| Field | Required | Default | Description |\n|-------|----------|---------|-------------|\n| `implement` | yes | -- | Role string for the implementing agent. Same syntax as the CLI: `<provider> [-m model] [--effort level] [--max-turns n] [--prefer-subagent model]` |\n| `review` | yes | -- | Role string for the reviewing agent |\n| `maxRounds` | no | `3` | Maximum review/fix rounds per ticket |\n| `minRounds` | no | `1` | Minimum rounds before a clean review can pass the ticket |\n\nA ticket passes when a round ends with no open findings and\nat least `minRounds` rounds have run. With `minRounds: 2`, a\nclean first round is followed by a second review before the\nticket merges. When the review in round `maxRounds` leaves\nfindings open, the ticket becomes `ready-for-human` (unresolved)\nwith its branch kept, and the fixer does not run after that\nfinal review.\n\nA missing file or a file with no `adversarial` key leaves\nbehavior unchanged. Invalid JSON, an `adversarial` value that\nis not an object, a missing role, or an invalid role string\nstops the run before any branch or worktree is created\n(exit 2).\n\nA role string with `--max-turns` or `--prefer-subagent` on a\nprovider that does not support them is not an error -- redeye\nwarns and drops the flag for that role, the same as the CLI\npath.\n\n\n## Command Line Arguments\n\nFlags:\n\n| Flag | Required | Default | Description |\n|------|----------|---------|-------------|\n| `[provider]` | no | -- | Agent harness to spawn (e.g. `claude`, `codex`, `pi`). Optional when `.redeye.json` sets `implement` -- the implement role's provider is used. A CLI provider overrides implement |\n| `[turns]` | no | -- | Max agentic turns per agent run (positional shorthand for `--max-turns`) |\n| `-m`, `--model` | no | -- | Model flag passed to the agent |\n| `--spec <name>` | no | auto | Feature name (resolves `.scratch/<name>/`) |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"returnCodeInterpretation":"No matches found","noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01V69rjtZRu1RtspVDNZce8Q","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
