{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFKzoz3MHfBkP1KhSx3z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0143C7gEo7tSRu7sQaBdN6La","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/nick/code/redeye.adversarial-review-02-run-with-the-implement-role/README.md","old_string":"A role string with `--max-turns` or `--prefer-subagent` on a","new_string":"With `adversarial` set, a bare `redeye` runs tickets with the\n`implement` role. A provider on the command line replaces the\nwhole `implement` role for that run (its flags do not carry\nover), and redeye logs one line saying so. Flags inside a role\nstring win for that role; run-wide flags such as `-m` or\n`--effort` fill in whatever the string leaves out, for both\nroles:\n\n```sh\n# .redeye.json: implement \"claude -m opus\", review \"pi\"\nredeye --effort high -m qwen\n# implement runs claude -m opus --effort high\n# review runs pi -m qwen --effort high\n```\n\nBoth role executables are checked before the run starts; a\nmissing one exits 2 before any branch is created. When both\nroles resolve to the same provider and model, redeye warns once\n(also in `--dry-run`) and runs anyway. Outside a git repo the\nloop does not run, and redeye logs that it was skipped.\n\nA role string with `--max-turns` or `--prefer-subagent` on a"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":960,"cache_read_input_tokens":99874,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":960},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fe82aa-8f32-4a13-8174-61fa0bc9b8df","uuid":"5685722e-655b-4ad3-a8bb-bf3a021b0e09","timestamp":"2026-11-21T03:01:52.007Z","request_id":"req_011ChFK