{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFL1XkmAMFt9Cjj9Xauo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MGtCFuV55LKUNX8GSGLJS2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"- In-place `runWaves` (outside a git repo) is the reduced path: no\"\"\"\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a,\"\"\"- `resolveRoles` in `src/config.ts` is the one place that decides\n  each role's provider and flags: a CLI provider replaces\n  `implement` whole, each role's own flags win, and run-wide CLI\n  flags fill in the rest. `runExecute` reads effort, max turns,\n  model and prefer-subagent from the resolved roles, never from\n  `argv` directly.\n\"\"\"+a)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nmkdir -p .redeye && cat > .redeye/notes.md <<'EOF'\n# Ticket 02: run with the implement role\n\nMost of this ticket was already on the branch (earlier US-004/US-006\ncommits): optional `[provider]`, `.check()` usage error, override log\nline, review preflight, same-model warning, dry-run lines, in-place\nskip log, and their CLI tests. I verified each and filled the gap.\n\nGap fixed (TDD, red then green):\n- Flag precedence was wrong: CLI `-m` beat the implement role's\n  model, the implement role's `--effort`/`--max-turns`/\n  `--prefer-subagent` were ignored, and the review role got no CLI\n  fill-in. Added `resolveRoles` and `sameModel` to src/config.ts\n  (unit tests in test/config.test.ts) and wired runExecute to them.\n- The same-model warning now compares the merged roles (e.g.\n  implement `claude`, review `claude -m opus`, CLI `-m opus` warns).\n- New CLI-run tests in test/integration.test.ts: bare run uses the\n  implement provider with role model winning over -m and CLI effort\n  filling in, review (fake pi) gets the CLI model; CLI provider\n  override in a real run logs the line and drops the role's model;\n  same-model warning appears once in a real run that goes ahead.\n\nReading of vague criteria: a CLI provider replaces the implement\nrole whole, so the role string's flags do not carry over to it.\n\nFiles: src/config.ts, src/index.ts, test/config.test.ts,\ntest/integration.test.ts, README.md, AGENTS.md.\n\nRunning a subset of integration tests: copy the file with chosen\ntitles switched to `test.only`, bundle with esbuild, run with\nGIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL pointing at a file with `useConfigOnly = true`.\nEOF\nnpm run build >/dev/null 2>&1; npm test > /tmp/redeye-02-test.log 2>&1; echo exit=$?; grep -E \"^# (tests|pass|fail)\" /tmp/redeye-02-test.log | tail -12; grep -n \"^not ok\" /tmp/redeye-02-test.log | head","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":448,"cache_read_input_tokens":101485,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":448},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fe82aa-8f32-4a13-8174-61fa0bc9b8df","uuid":"4e414c35-9d4c-426e-acf1-ede15a641aa6","timestamp":"2026-11-21T03:02:07.243Z","request_id":"req_011ChFL1Xc5QA9h4TxM52peC","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MGtCFuV55LKUNX8GSGLJS2":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/redeye.adversarial-review-02-run-with-the-implement-role && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"- In-place `runWaves` (outside a git repo) is the reduced path: no\"\"\"\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a,\"\"\"- `resolveRoles` in `src/config.ts` is the one place that decides\n  each role's provider and flags: a CLI provider replaces\n  `implement` whole, each role's own flags win, and run-wide CLI\n  flags fill in the rest. `runExecute` reads effort, max turns,\n  model and prefer-subagent from the resolved roles, never from\n  `argv` directly.\n\"\"\"+a)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nmkdi