{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFLJHRX91QMEdvubcKS8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Ticket 02 is done. The full `npm test` run passed (exit 0) and lint is clean.\n\nMost of the ticket was already on the branch from earlier commits: the optional `[provider]`, the unchanged usage error, the override log line, the review-executable preflight, the same-model warning, the dry-run lines and the in-place \"skipped\" log. Each already had a CLI test.\n\n**The bug I fixed:** flag precedence was wrong. A CLI `-m` beat the model in the implement role string. The implement role's `--effort`, `--max-turns` and `--prefer-subagent` were ignored. The review role got none of the run-wide flags filled in.\n\n**What changed:**\n1. `src/config.ts` has two new functions. `resolveRoles` works out each role's provider and flags. A CLI provider replaces the whole implement role, each role's own flags win, and CLI flags fill in the rest, for both roles. `sameModel` compares two roles by provider basename and model.\n2. `runExecute` in `src/index.ts` now reads model, effort, max turns and prefer-subagent from those resolved roles. It passes the resolved review role on to `runWavesIsolated` but does not start a reviewer. The same-model warning now compares the resolved roles. Before, implement `claude`, review `claude -m opus` and `-m opus` on the command line gave no warning; now it warns.\n3. New unit tests in `test/config.test.ts`. Three new full-run CLI tests in `test/integration.test.ts`:\n   - A bare `redeye` runs the implement provider. The role's model beats `-m`, the CLI `--effort` fills in, and the reviewer gets the CLI model.\n   - A CLI provider overrides implement in a real run and logs that it did.\n   - The same-model warning appears once in a real run, and the run still goes ahead.\n\n   The new tests failed against the old code for the expected reasons and pass now.\n4. The README now explains which flags win, the startup checks and the in-place skip. `AGENTS.md` has one line saying `resolveRoles` is the single place roles get decided. My notes are in `.redeye/notes.md`.\n\n**One decision:** a provider given on the command line replaces the implement role entirely, so flags from the implement string do not carry over to it. The ticket didn't say either way. This is the more literal reading of \"overrides `implement`\", and the new override test checks it.\n\n[x] A bare `redeye` in a repo whose `.redeye.json` configures `adversarial` runs tickets with the `implement` provider and model\n[x] A provider on the command line overrides `implement` for that run and logs that it did\n[x] A CLI flag the role string leaves out applies to that role; a flag set in the role string wins over the CLI flag\n[x] A missing `review` executable makes the run exit 2 before any branch is created\n[x] `implement` and `review` with the same provider and model produce the same-model warning in a run and in `--dry-run`\n[x] `--dry-run` says when a command-line provider overrides `implement`\n[x] A bare `redeye` with no `.redeye.json` still gives today's usage error"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":306,"cache_read_input_tokens":103239,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":306},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fe82aa-8f32-4a13-8174-61fa0bc9b8df","uuid":"2dcd2b37-b7ed-4c41-9e83-0f59450d7b68","timestamp":"2026-11-21T03:05:52.673Z","request_id":"req_011ChFLJGvFySpmDzEF9CzGk"}
